VP8 decoding and encoding through the Termux:VA bridge (debian-livecd-termux).

Gallium has no VP8 video format, so this adds PIPE_VIDEO_FORMAT_VP8 and
PIPE_VIDEO_PROFILE_VP8 (VAProfileVP8Version0_3) for the bridge alone.

Decode: VA-API slice data starts at the first partition. picture_vp8.c keeps
the picture and slice parameters and rebuilds the 3-byte frame tag (and the
7-byte key-frame start code and size) MediaCodec needs in front of it. The
first partition's size follows from the slice data size and the coefficient
partition sizes. Every frame is marked shown, as each VA picture fills its
target surface.

Encode: VP8 reuses the VP9 encoder descriptor (bitrate, frame rate, visible
size, key frame, coded buffer) and the new append-only CODEC_VP8_ENC (14).

Both are offered only when the daemon lists a hardware codec: decoders in
<socket>.decoders, encoders in <socket>.encoders (a missing list does not
count for VP8). TERMUX_VA_DISABLE_VP8=1 hides both.

